Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Chern-Simons IBL Algebras", "GuideTitle",
 CellID->942062912,ExpressionUUID->"a3a3c038-ca24-47b7-9945-83f1c1312fe3"],

Cell["\<\
An involutive bi-Lie infinity structure on the cyclic words of a graded \
alphabet with a pairing, in both the graded exterior and the graded symmetric \
convention. The alphabet is data, not global state: a pairing object carries \
the degrees of the particles and the values of the pairing, and every \
operation takes it as its last argument. The pairing that matters \
geometrically comes from Poincare duality, so the paclet also builds it \
\[LongDash] from a Sullivan minimal model with a volume form, through the \
test for Hodge type and the nondegenerate quotient, to the finite-dimensional \
Poincare duality algebra and the canonical Maurer-Cartan element its triple \
product carries. When the model is not formal that algebra carries a \
differential too, and the alphabet carries it into the operation q(1,1,0), \
the first summand of the Beilinson-Drinfeld operator and of the twisted \
differential.\
\>", "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"]
}, Open  ]],

